      <p class="section__text">
        The LDC (Least Developed Country) window for Bangladesh duty-free access to Europe closes in November 2026. After this date, Bangladesh will graduate to developing country status and face standard MFN duties. This creates genuine urgency for brands to establish Bangladesh manufacturing relationships now and lock in current duty rates. Brands that wait until 2026 will face immediate cost increases of 12% on EU imports. Establishing production in Bangladesh today secures duty-free access through the transition period.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Bangladesh has evolved beyond its reputation as a low-cost, low-quality option. The industry's post-2013 safety reforms - driven by the Accord and Alliance initiatives - have created one of the world's safest garment manufacturing environments. Leading factories like SDF invest in worker training, modern equipment, and sustainable practices. The certification coverage in Bangladesh now exceeds China in many categories, particularly for organic and sustainable materials. Brands seeking <a href="/clothing-manufacturer-bangladesh" class="link">clothing manufacturers in Bangladesh</a> find partners that match or exceed Chinese quality standards at lower costs.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        The service model also differs. SDF Clothing offers <a href="/private-label-manufacturer" class="link">private label manufacturing</a> with end-to-end support including fabric sourcing, pattern making, sampling, production, and quality control. This <a href="/full-package-production" class="link">full package production</a> approach reduces complexity for brands that lack in-house technical teams. While Chinese factories can offer similar services, they typically charge premium rates for full-package support. Bangladesh's value proposition includes comprehensive service at competitive pricing.
      </p>
      <p class="section__text">
        Certification coverage is a critical differentiator. SDF is a <a href="/certifications" class="link">GOTS and OEKO-TEX certified factory</a> with 13 verifiable certifications spanning quality, social compliance, and environmental standards. Matching this certification breadth in China requires working with top-tier factories that command premium pricing. For brands targeting sustainability-focused consumers, Bangladesh's certification coverage provides marketing advantages at lower costs.
